  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/site100-300.html",
  "prefLabel": "Site 202.19 Burden and Standard of Proof",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Site 202.19 Burden and Standard of Proof.\n\n(a) The party asserting a proposition shall bear the burden of proving the proposition by a preponderance of the evidence.\n\n(b) An applicant for a certificate of site and facility shall bear the burden of proving facts sufficient for the committee or subcommittee, as applicable, to make the findings required by RSA 162-H:16.\n\n(c) In a hearing held to determine whether a certificate, license, permit or other approval that has already been issued should be suspended, revoked or not renewed, the committee or subcommittee, as applicable, shall make its decision based on a preponderance of the evidence in the record.\n\nSource. #9183-A, eff 6-17-08; ss by #10993, eff 12-16-15",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/site100-300.html"
